The divergence between the **prediction (down)** and the prevailing **""Strong Uptrend""** is logical. We are anticipating a **trend reversal/pullback within a larger uptrend**. This is a common technical occurrence where an asset becomes overextended and must correct to shed overbought conditions and gather strength for its next potential leg up. The absence of a bullish news catalyst to justify a continued surge at these levels increases the likelihood of this consolidation/pullback phase beginning in the coming week.

